<!-- ================= THU ================= -->
<section id="thu" data-date="2026-08-06">
<div class="dayhead"><h2>Day 1 · Thu Aug 6 — Travel In</h2>
<div class="meta">GSP → DEN → COD · <b>land 10:43 PM</b> · sleep: Bleistein</div></div>

<div class="kit"><b>Today’s kit</b>Carry-on: chargers + one USB-C cable · Turo app signed in, <b style="display:inline;font-size:inherit;letter-spacing:0;text-transform:none;font-family:inherit">license uploaded</b> · Grant conf screenshot (20977608) · offline maps, park app, playlists downloaded · headlamp packed</div>
<div class="stop"><input class="ck" type="checkbox" id="thu0"><label class="check" for="thu0">✓</label>
<details><summary><span class="time" data-m="975" data-e="1075"><small class="tl">dep</small><b>4:15</b><small>PM</small><em><small class="tl">arr</small><span class="ev">5:55</span></em></span>
<span class="stop-main"><span class="title">Depart GSP — UA1866 to Denver</span><span class="flow">1 hr 40 flight → Denver</span></span></summary>
<div class="body"><p>Land DEN 5:55 PM. Offline maps, park app, playlists, podcasts downloaded before boarding. Grant confirmation screenshot in photos: <b>20977608</b>.</p></div></details></div>

<div class="stop"><input class="ck" type="checkbox" id="thu1"><label class="check" for="thu1">✓</label>
<details><summary><span class="time" data-m="1075" data-e="1265"><small class="tl">arr</small><b>5:55</b><small>PM</small><em><small class="tl">lv</small><span class="ev">9:05</span></em></span>
<span class="stop-main"><span class="title">Denver layover — eat a real dinner</span>
<span class="chips"><span class="chip meal">Dinner</span><span class="chip drive">3 hrs</span></span><span class="flow">3 hr 10 layover + dinner · <em>board 9:05, fly → Cody</em></span></span></summary>
<div class="body"><p>Nothing in Cody is open when you land. This is dinner. Board UA5132 at 9:05.</p></div></details></div>

<div class="stop"><input class="ck" type="checkbox" id="thu2"><label class="check" for="thu2">✓</label>
<details><summary><span class="time" data-m="1363" data-e="1385"><small class="tl">arr</small><b>10:43</b><small>PM</small><em><small class="tl">lv</small><span class="ev">11:05</span></em></span>
<span class="stop-main"><span class="title">Land Cody — grab the truck (contactless)</span>
<span class="chips"><span class="chip drive">5 min</span></span><span class="flow">~20 min truck pickup + photos · <em>5 min drive → Bleistein</em></span></span></summary>
<div class="body"><p>GMC Sierra 1500 waiting at the airport — Amber texts the exact spot + key location day-of (plate <b>11T482K</b>). <b>Before driving: full walkaround photos/video + odometer shot in the Turo app</b>, even at 11 PM — night pickups are exactly when you skip this and regret it. Body clock says 12:43 AM.</p><p>If energized: Walmart run tonight — cooler, ice, water, sandwich stuff, thermos, snacks.</p><a class="maplink" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=1822+Bleistein+Ave+Cody+WY">⌖ 1822 Bleistein Ave</a></div></details></div>

<div class="stop"><input class="ck" type="checkbox" id="thu3"><label class="check" for="thu3">✓</label>
<details><summary><span class="time" data-m="1410"><small class="tl">at</small><b>11:30</b><small>PM</small></span>
<span class="stop-main"><span class="title">Bed. No alarm.</span><span class="flow">lights out</span></span></summary>
<div class="body"><p>Tomorrow starts when it starts. Errands first, mountains after.</p></div></details></div>
</section>

<!-- ================= FRI ================= -->
<section id="fri" data-date="2026-08-07" data-shift>
<div class="dayhead"><h2>Day 2 · Fri Aug 7 — The High Loop: Beartooth → Lamar</h2>
<div class="meta">~220 mi · <b>~6 hrs driving</b> · home ~10:15 PM · sleep: Bleistein</div>
<div class="shiftrow"></div>
<div class="shnote">Slept in? Pick a shift — every time below moves with it. Sunset-tied stops stay put.</div></div>

<div class="kit"><b>Today’s kit</b>Bear spray (buy first) · cooler + ice + lunch/dinner makings · water jugs · grandpa's binoculars · fleece + beanie (Lamar goes cold at dusk) · rain shell · headlamp · camp chair · sunscreen + hat · bug spray · thermos · full tank</div>
<div class="stop"><input class="ck" type="checkbox" id="fri0"><label class="check" for="fri0">✓</label>
<details><summary><span class="time" data-m="450" data-e="510"><small class="tl">arr</small><b>7:30</b><small>AM</small><em><small class="tl">lv</small><span class="ev">8:30</span></em></span>
<span class="stop-main"><span class="title">Errands run</span>
<span class="chips"><span class="chip meal">Breakfast · house</span></span><span class="flow">1 hr errands + load-up · <em>then roll out</em></span></span></summary>
<div class="body"><p>One Walmart mission (~25 min, ~$110–140), then gas. If Thursday-night energy allowed an early run, this is just the gap-fill.</p>
<div class="lookfor"><b>Cooler + drinks</b>Cheap cooler ($15–25, gets abandoned Tuesday) · 2 bags ice (restock Sat) · water gallons ×3–4 · electrolyte packets / Gatorade · Lamar truck-bed drinks</div>
<div class="lookfor"><b>Sandwich operation</b>Bread or tortillas · deli meat + cheese · PB + jam · apples/clementines · trail mix · jerky · chips · granola/protein bars (glovebox stash) · grab-breakfast for Sunday 6:30 AM at Grant (pastries / oats cups)</div>
<div class="lookfor"><b>Coffee kit</b>Thermos ($10, if the house is bare) · instant coffee you can respect (Via or similar — the Sunday huckleberry latte is the reward)</div>
<div class="lookfor"><b>Safety + sundries</b><b style="display:inline;font-size:inherit;letter-spacing:0;text-transform:none;font-family:inherit">Bear spray ~$50</b> (if Walmart's wall looks stale, Sunlight Sports downtown opens at 9) · sunscreen SPF 30+ · SPF chapstick · small bug spray · blister bandages / moleskin + ibuprofen · wet wipes + paper towels · zip-locks (sandwiches + phone at the Firehole swim)</div>
<div class="lookfor"><b>Judgment calls</b>Camp chair $10–15 (four hours in Lamar says yes) · cheap sandals/water shoes if unpacked · road candy for Chief Joseph at 9:45 PM</div>
<p>Then: <b>full tank</b> on the way out of town.</p></div></details></div>

<div class="stop"><input class="ck" type="checkbox" id="fri1"><label class="check" for="fri1">✓</label>
<details><summary><span class="time" data-m="510" data-e="565"><small class="tl">dep</small><b>8:30</b><small>AM</small><em><small class="tl">arr</small><span class="ev">9:25</span></em></span>
<span class="stop-main"><span class="title">Depart — Chief Joseph Hwy</span>
<span class="chips"><span class="chip drive">55 min</span></span><span class="flow"><em>55 min drive → Dead Indian Pass</em></span></span></summary>
<div class="body"><p>North on WY-120, west on 296. Fresh chip seal this summer — easy on loose gravel.</p></div></details></div>

<div class="stop"><input class="ck" type="checkbox" id="fri2"><label class="check" for="fri2">✓</label>
<details><summary><span class="time" data-m="565" data-e="590"><small class="tl">arr</small><b>9:25</b><small>AM</small><em><small class="tl">lv</small><span class="ev">9:50</span></em></span>
<span class="stop-main"><span class="title">Dead Indian Pass Overlook</span>
<span class="chips"><span class="chip">20 min stop</span></span><span class="flow">25 min at the overlook · <em>60 min drive → Beartooth Pass</em></span></span></summary>
<div class="body"><p>Walk it, don't just shoot it. Clarks Fork canyon and Sunlight Basin below — the country the Nez Perce ran in 1877. The wall to the northwest is where you're headed.</p><p><b>Beta:</b> Big paved lot right at the summit — park anywhere, walk the low stone-wall rim to the interpretive signs at the far end. Best photo angle is from the little knob just past the signs. 15–20 min is the right dose; the road down the other side is the show’s second act.</p><a class="maplink" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=44.7448,-109.3862">⌖ Open in Maps</a></div></details></div>

<div class="stop"><input class="ck" type="checkbox" id="fri4"><label class="check" for="fri4">✓</label>
<details><summary><span class="time" data-m="650" data-e="710"><small class="tl">arr</small><b>10:50</b><small>AM</small><em><small class="tl">lv</small><span class="ev">11:50</span></em></span>
<span class="stop-main"><span class="title">Beartooth Pass — 10,947 ft</span>
<span class="chips"><span class="chip drive">→ 60 min</span><span class="chip">a full hour on foot</span></span><span class="flow">a full hour on the tundra · <em>25 min drive → Rock Creek Vista</em></span></span></summary>
<div class="body"><div class="lookfor"><b>Look for</b>Mountain goats on the crags · pikas squeaking in talus · peak wildflowers · touchable snowfields</div><p>The "another planet" report. Wander off the pullout into the tundra — most people give this four minutes. Can be 45°F and blowing while Cody bakes; the layer lives in the truck. (Cruise past Beartooth Lake without stopping — its shore walk is Monday’s show with mom.)</p><p><b>Beta:</b> Two pull-offs flank the actual summit sign — use the bigger one on the west side. Walk north off the pavement onto the tundra (it’s open travel up here, stay on rock/gravel where you can). Scan the crags south of the road for goats and listen for pika ‘eep’s in every talus pile. The West Summit overlook a mile further has the classic switchback-view pullout if you want one more stop.</p><div class="trail"><b class="h">Trail · no formal trail needed</b>Park the pullout and wander the open tundra 10–20 min on rock and gravel (stay off the fragile plant mats). Want a marked path instead? The Gardner Lake trailhead 0.5 mi down the east side drops to an alpine lake — but save the legs for Trout Lake this afternoon.</div><a class="maplink" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=44.9705,-109.4655">⌖ Open in Maps</a></div></details></div>

<div class="stop"><input class="ck" type="checkbox" id="fri5"><label class="check" for="fri5">✓</label>
<details><summary><span class="time" data-m="735" data-e="750"><small class="tl">arr</small><b>12:15</b><small>PM</small><em><small class="tl">lv</small><span class="ev">12:30</span></em></span>
<span class="stop-main"><span class="title">Rock Creek Vista — TURNAROUND</span>
<span class="chips"><span class="chip drive">→ 25 min</span></span><span class="flow">15 min at the rail · <em>55 min drive → Cooke City</em></span></span></summary>
<div class="body"><p><b>~15 min here</b>, then the hour back over the pass — Cooke City lunch at 1:25. 2,000-ft look down the glacial canyon. This is the top of the day — no Red Lodge descent. Retrace west.</p><p><b>Beta:</b> Big lot, and the overlook is a 300-yard paved path — easiest jaw-drop of the trip. Look straight down Rock Creek’s U-shaped glacial canyon; the road you’re NOT taking today snakes down its wall. Restrooms here — use them.</p><a class="maplink" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=45.0517,-109.4046">⌖ Open in Maps</a></div></details></div>

<div class="stop"><input class="ck" type="checkbox" id="fri6"><label class="check" for="fri6">✓</label>
<details><summary><span class="time" data-m="805" data-e="850"><small class="tl">arr</small><b>1:25</b><small>PM</small><em><small class="tl">lv</small><span class="ev">2:10</span></em></span>
<span class="stop-main"><span class="title">Cooke City — lunch · GAS · bathroom</span>
<span class="chips"><span class="chip meal">Lunch</span><span class="chip drive">→ 55 min</span><span class="chip">Miners Saloon</span></span><span class="flow">45 min lunch + gas · <em>25 min drive → NE Entrance</em></span></span></summary>
<div class="body"><p>Sit-down burger, no rush. <b>Last fuel before home.</b> The full pre-Lamar checklist, handled by a frontier town of ~100.</p><p><b>Beta:</b> Everything is on the one main street: Miners Saloon mid-town on the north side (order at the bar, cash preferred historically), gas at the stations on either end of town — hit whichever’s open, they keep frontier hours. Fill the water bottles too; next reliable everything is home.</p><a class="maplink" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Miners+Saloon+Cooke+City+MT">⌖ Open in Maps</a></div></details></div>

<div class="stop"><input class="ck" type="checkbox" id="fri7"><label class="check" for="fri7">✓</label>
<details><summary><span class="time" data-m="875" data-e="880"><small class="tl">arr</small><b>2:35</b><small>PM</small><em><small class="tl">lv</small><span class="ev">2:40</span></em></span>
<span class="stop-main"><span class="title">Northeast Entrance</span>
<span class="chips"><span class="chip drive">→ 25 min</span></span><span class="flow">5 min at the gate · <em>20 min drive → Trout Lake</em></span></span></summary>
<div class="body"><p>$35 pass (7 days, keep the receipt) if not already bought. Quietest gate in the park.</p></div></details></div>

<div class="stop"><input class="ck" type="checkbox" id="fri8"><label class="check" for="fri8">✓</label>
<details><summary><span class="time" data-m="900" data-e="975"><small class="tl">arr</small><b>3:00</b><small>PM</small><em><small class="tl">lv</small><span class="ev">4:15</span></em></span>
<span class="stop-main"><span class="title">Trout Lake</span>
<span class="chips"><span class="chip drive">→ 20 min</span><span class="chip">¾ mi steep</span><span class="chip">30 min at the water</span></span><span class="flow">1 hr 15 hike + lakeside sit · <em>15 min drive → Lamar</em></span></span></summary>
<div class="body"><div class="lookfor"><b>Look for</b>Big cutthroat cruising the shallows · otters (reliable spot) · spray on hip</div><p>Steep climb through Douglas fir to absurdly clear water. First real payoff of the Hokas. Sit and watch the fish patrol.</p><p><b>Beta:</b> Trailhead is a small unsigned-feeling pullout on the north side of the road — if you hit Pebble Creek you went ~1.5 mi too far. The climb is steep but short (15 min of work). At the top, go LEFT around the lake — the inlet creek on the far side is where cutthroat stack and otters hunt. The downed logs along the west shore are the sitting spots.</p><div class="trail"><b class="h">Trail · Trout Lake Trail · 1.2–1.5 mi RT · ~380 ft · 45–75 min</b>Switchback up through the firs ~15–20 min to the lake. At the top take the shoreline path LEFT (clockwise): ~0.6 mi around, hitting the inlet creek on the far side (stacked cutthroat, otter territory) and the west-shore logs before closing the loop at the outlet. Same steep trail back down.</div><a class="maplink" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=44.8996,-110.1223">⌖ Open in Maps</a></div></details></div>

