<div class="body"><div class="lookfor"><b>Look for</b>Dragon's Mouth growling (steam collapsing in the cave) · bison lounging on warm ground</div><p>The park's most acidic, gassiest ground. Do the hillside stairs, not just the roadside pots.</p><p><b>Beta:</b> Lot is on the west side of the road — Dragon’s Mouth is 100 yards from your bumper, growling. Walk the loop CLOCKWISE: up the stairs to Churning Caldron and Sour Lake first, down past Black Dragon’s Caldron. Bison bed down on the warm ground here and have right-of-way everywhere — 25 yards minimum, reroute around them.</p><div class="trail"><b class="h">Trail · Mud Volcano Loop · 0.7 mi · ~35 min</b>Clockwise from the lot: stairs up to Churning Caldron and Sour Lake on the ridge, then down past Black Dragon’s Caldron and Mud Geyser, finishing at Dragon’s Mouth beside the parking.</div><a class="maplink" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=44.6249,-110.4382">⌖ Open in Maps</a></div></details></div>

<div class="stop"><input class="ck" type="checkbox" id="sat3"><label class="check" for="sat3">✓</label>
<details><summary><span class="time" data-m="645" data-e="795"><small class="tl">arr</small><b>10:45</b><small>AM</small><em><small class="tl">lv</small><span class="ev">1:15</span><small class="m2">PM</small></em></span>
