<span class="chips"><span class="chip drive">→ 20 min</span><span class="chip">~2.5 hrs</span></span><span class="flow">2 hr 30 walking the rims · <em>12 min drive → Dunraven Pass</em></span></span></summary>
<div class="body"><div class="lookfor"><b>Look for</b>Ospreys nesting on canyon spires · mid-morning rainbows in the falls mist</div><p><b>South rim:</b> Artist Point (the postcard — 308-ft falls in yellow-pink hydrothermally cooked rock), then the <b>Point Sublime trail</b> — the ¾-mile 95% of visitors skip.</p><p><b>North rim</b> (10-min drive): Red Rock / Lookout Point, Inspiration Point, then the <b>Brink of the Lower Falls</b> switchbacks — stand on top of the falls as the river goes over under your feet. Steep back up; the Hokas' first real test.</p><p><b>Beta:</b> Sequence: South Rim Drive to the Artist Point lot (biggest in the area), do the Point Sublime out-and-back from the far end of the viewing deck, then drive back around to the one-way North Rim Drive — it serves Brink of the Lower Falls first, then Lookout/Red Rock, then Inspiration Point. The Brink trail drops ~600 ft in switchbacks; count on 20 sweaty minutes back up.</p><div class="trail"><b class="h">Trail · Canyon rims · 4 short walks · ~3.5 mi total · ~2.5 hr</b>1) Artist Point: 200-yd paved path from the lot, then the Point Sublime Trail east from the far end of the deck — 1.25 mi one-way, level rim walking; out-and-back as far as it’s giving (~50 min full RT). 2) Drive to the one-way North Rim Dr: Brink of the Lower Falls Trail, 0.7 mi RT, ~600 ft of switchbacks, 35–40 min. 3) Lookout Point (steps from its lot); the Red Rock Point drop below it is 0.4 mi RT / ~30 min — optional, skip if the legs are budgeting for Washburn. 4) Inspiration Point: 5–10 min from the last lot.</div><a class="maplink" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=44.7201,-110.4794">⌖ Artist Point</a></div></details></div>

<div class="stop"><input class="ck" type="checkbox" id="sat4"><label class="check" for="sat4">✓</label>
<details><summary><span class="time" data-m="810" data-e="1000"><small class="tl">arr</small><b>1:30</b><small>PM</small><em><small class="tl">lv</small><span class="ev">4:40</span></em></span>
<span class="stop-main"><span class="title">Mount Washburn — summit lunch</span>
<span class="chips"><span class="chip meal">Lunch · summit</span><span class="chip drive">→ 12 min</span><span class="chip">6.4 mi RT</span><span class="chip">down by ~4:45</span></span><span class="flow">3 hr 10 hike + summit lunch · <em>20 min drive → Hayden</em></span></span></summary>
<div class="body"><div class="lookfor"><b>Look for</b>Bighorn sheep near the summit (resident band) · marmots · storm clouds after 2 = descend</div><p>~1,400 ft on a wide old road-grade. <b>Eat lunch on top, 30 unhurried minutes</b> — 10,243 ft, the whole park in 360°, Tetons on the horizon. This week's forecast shows 0% storm chance, so the afternoon summit is safe; if clouds are stacking by noon anyway, invert the day — hike first, canyon after.</p><p><b>Beta:</b> Dunraven Pass lot sits right on the road summit and fills by late morning — at your 1:30 arrival, circle patiently or use the overflow pullouts just north. The trail is the old road grade the whole way: wide, steady, impossible to lose. Bighorns usually hang on the ridgeline just below the summit switchbacks. The fire lookout on top has a public observation room, restroom, and windbreak — lunch inside if the wind’s rude.</p><div class="trail"><b class="h">Trail · Mount Washburn Trail via Dunraven Pass · 6.4 mi RT · ~1,400 ft · ~3 hr with lunch</b>One obvious old road-grade the entire way — broad switchbacks up the south ridge, no junctions to miss (a spur merges in from the Chittenden Road side near the top; just keep climbing). Budget ~1 hr 45 up, 30 on the summit, ~1 hr down. Views open at the first switchback and never stop.</div><p><i>Sacrifice-order note: skipping the summit entirely is pre-approved. Canyon + early check-in is still a great day. The crown jewel is tomorrow regardless.</i></p><a class="maplink" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=44.7796,-110.4494">⌖ Dunraven Pass trailhead</a></div></details></div>

<div class="stop"><input class="ck" type="checkbox" id="sat5"><label class="check" for="sat5">✓</label>
<details><summary><span class="time" data-m="1020" data-e="1055"><small class="tl">arr</small><b>5:00</b><small>PM</small><em><small class="tl">lv</small><span class="ev">5:35</span></em></span>
