<div class="body"><p>Deluxe Lodge, 1 Queen. Check-in desk after 4. Solve tomorrow's coffee tonight (thermos + cooler — nothing opens early).</p><p><b>Swim #1 (optional): the lakeshore plunge.</b> Yellowstone Lake runs ~55–60° — this is a 30-second in-and-out off the Grant shore before dinner settles, not a swim. Cold-shock rules: waist-deep, dunk, out, towel, bragging rights forever.</p><p><b>Beta:</b> Check-in is the registration building as you enter the village. For the plunge + sky show: the beach by the amphitheater/marina area is a 5-minute walk east from the lodge buildings — sand entry, no rocks. Face south over the water for the Milky Way core; give your eyes 10 dark minutes and it triples.</p><p><b>~10:00 PM: walk to the lakeshore and look up.</b> One of the darkest skies in the lower 48 — the Milky Way core is out. Ten minutes minimum. Then bed.</p><a class="maplink" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=24+Rainbow+Loop+Grant+Village+Yellowstone">⌖ 24 Rainbow Loop</a></div></details></div>
